 # NextAuth Migration — Implementation Plan

## Goal
Replace Supabase Auth with **NextAuth (Auth.js v5)** for:
- Direct Google OAuth via GCP (no Supabase middleman)
- Password hashing via `bcrypt` (not Supabase's internal hashing)
- JWT sessions signed with `AUTH_SECRET`

Supabase remains as the **database only** (accessed via `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`).

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Browser -->|"Login"| NextAuth["Auth.js v5"]
    NextAuth <-->|"OAuth 2.0"| Google["Google GCP"]
    NextAuth -->|"JWT Session"| ServerActions["Server Actions"]
    ServerActions <-->|"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"| Supabase["Supabase (DB only)"]
```

---

## Execution Plan

### Phase 1: Install & Configure NextAuth

#### 1.1 Install `next-auth@beta` (Auth.js v5)

#### 1.2 [NEW] `src/auth.ts` — NextAuth configuration
- Google provider with `AUTH_GOOGLE_ID` / `AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET`
- Credentials provider for email/password (uses `bcrypt.compare`)
- `signIn` callback: validate `@nirmauni.ac.in` domain
- `jwt` callback: attach `profileId`, `status`, `isMembershipComplete` to token
- `session` callback: expose profile data to client

#### 1.3 [NEW] `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`
- NextAuth catch-all API route handler

#### 1.4 [MODIFY] `.env`
- Add `NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000` (required by Auth.js v5)

---

### Phase 2: Database Schema Update

#### 2.1 New migration: `00003_nextauth_migration.sql`
```sql
-- Add password_hash column for email/password users
ALTER TABLE profiles ADD COLUMN password_hash TEXT;

-- Remove the auth.users trigger (NextAuth manages users directly)
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS on_auth_user_created ON auth.users;

-- Remove FK constraint to auth.users (profiles now stand alone)
ALTER TABLE profiles DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS profiles_pkey;
ALTER TABLE profiles ADD PRIMARY KEY (id);
-- Note: profiles.id will be a UUID we generate ourselves
```

> [!WARNING]
> This migration decouples `profiles` from `auth.users`. The `profiles` table becomes fully self-managed. Existing rows (if any) in `auth.users` will be orphaned. This is fine since we haven't launched yet.

---

### Phase 3: Rewrite Auth Layer

#### 3.1 [MODIFY] `src/utils/supabase/server.ts`
- Switch from `ANON_KEY` to `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`
- Remove cookie-based auth (NextAuth handles sessions)
- Simple admin client for DB queries only

#### 3.2 [DELETE] `src/utils/supabase/client.ts`
- No more client-side Supabase access (all data goes through Server Actions)

#### 3.3 [REWRITE] `src/app/auth/actions.ts`
| Function | Change |
|----------|--------|
| `signInWithGoogle()` | → `signIn('google')` from NextAuth |
| `signInWithEmail()` | → `signIn('credentials', { email, password })` from NextAuth |
| `signUp()` | → Hash password with `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`, INSERT into `profiles` directly |
| `completeRegistration()` | → Get session via `auth()`, update profile via service-role Supabase |
| `signOut()` | → `signOut()` from NextAuth |

#### 3.4 [DELETE] `src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`
- NextAuth handles OAuth callbacks at `/api/auth/callback/google` automatically

#### 3.5 [REWRITE] `src/utils/supabase/middleware.ts`
- Replace Supabase session check with NextAuth `auth()` call
- Keep the 3-tier routing logic (public → auth-only → protected)
- Query profile status via service-role Supabase client

#### 3.6 [MODIFY] `src/middleware.ts` (root)
- Wire up to new middleware function

